Ticket **#4471** merged 412 unique date reports and marked them known as one parser bug.
`causes.ts` splits those reports by tenant locale and booking form into **two** causes.
Each cause needs its own ticket; intake tags alone are not the cause.

<Callout>
#4471 is not one problem. File one ticket per cause; keep the report count on each ticket.
</Callout>

## Causes in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets filed

Report counts stay in `CauseTable` above. One GitHub issue per cause; each body states how many reports that cause covers.

- `parser` — [issue #2](https://github.com/arymasheusky-rgb/mega-ai-course/issues/2): shared parser reads month first; day-first tenants get flipped dates (app, email, and non-hint form paths).
- `hint` — [issue #3](https://github.com/arymasheusky-rgb/mega-ai-course/issues/3): booking-v3 shows `MM/DD/YYYY`; day-first people type that on the form; the form still reads day-first. Form + booking-v3 only.

## Lessons

- Merge on subject alone packs different causes into one ticket.
- Cause comes from tenant locale and form (`causes.ts`), not from `meta.intakeTag`.
- A number the data can compute belongs in a component (`CauseTable`), not typed into prose alone.

